# NPClaude speech: words. The format and every fact and word are described in basics.speech.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The word book. [word_prompt] is the question (a full sentence); [word] the word they just learned.

== ask_word ==
[word_prompt]
Can I ask you something odd? [word_prompt]
I've been wondering... [word_prompt]
Ooh, quick question! [word_prompt]   {extrovert, w=2}
Help me out. [word_prompt]           {rude, w=2}
You seem clever. [word_prompt]       {polite, w=2}
I collect words, you know. [word_prompt] {curious, w=3}

== word_whose ==
[word.cap]. Is that just for me, or something anyone could say?
[word.cap]! Is that our word, or can I tell people?
Can I share [word], or is it just ours? {nosy, w=3}
[word.cap]... I like it. Just mine, or everyone's? {w=1}

== word_learned ==
[word.cap]. I like it!
[word.cap]! I'll remember that.
[word.cap]. Ha! What a word.         {lighthearted, w=2}
[word.cap]. Very proper.             {proper, w=2}
[word.cap]... got it. Thanks.        {introvert, w=2}
[word.cap]. Our secret, then.        {personal=yes, w=3}
I'm going to tell EVERYONE about [word]. {personal=no, nosy, w=4}
I'm going to tell everyone about [word]. {personal=no, extrovert, w=3}
Fine. [word.cap]. Can I go now?      {rude, w=2}

== no_words ==
I don't know any special words. Teach me one sometime?
Words? Just the usual ones.
Nothing fancy. Teach me something!   {curious, w=3}
